From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:45:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] presentation: browse cells skip per-frame paging reads
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A browse panorama fling spent 2-11 ms in layout on the slow frames. Each cell
read LazyPagingItems.get, which subscribes that composition to the whole paging
snapshot and records a prefetch hint. The key lambda called peek on every
getKey. PanoramaMasonry.getIndex walked the list, and the item provider built
a new interval list on every call.

Manga cells and the loading row now have their own content types. The cell
reads the row with peek inside derivedStateOf, and calls get once from a
SideEffect so the next page still loads. Keys are taken once from the snapshot.
getIndex uses a map built with the interval content, and the provider is reused
while that content is current.

与 anikku-harmony 同病（同一段代码 / 同一套网格），Anikku 侧待移植。
